    <h2>Generated members, by declaration</h2>
    <p>What the generator adds to your partial class, for each thing you declare.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>You declare</th><th>Generated</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexStore]</code> on <code>partial class Foo</code></td>
                    <td>
                        <code>partial class Foo : BlexStoreBase</code>,
                        <code>override string Name</code>,
                        <code>override JsonObject SerializeState()</code>,
                        <code>override void DeserializeState(JsonObject)</code>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexStore(Persist = true)]</code></td>
                    <td><code>override bool Persist =&gt; true</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexState] private T _foo;</code></td>
                    <td><code>public T Foo { get; set; }</code> - the setter routes through <code>SetState</code>; the field is included in both snapshot methods</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexComputed] T ComputeFoo()</code></td>
                    <td><code>public T Foo { get; }</code> plus <code>__FooValid</code> / <code>__FooValue</code>, and an entry in <code>InvalidateComputed()</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexAction] void OnFoo(A a)</code></td>
                    <td><code>public void Foo(A a)</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexAction] Task OnFoo(A a)</code></td>
                    <td><code>public Task Foo(A a)</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexEffect] Task OnFoo(A a)</code></td>
                    <td>
                        <code>public Task Foo(A a)</code>,
                        <code>public bool FooIsLoading</code>,
                        <code>public Exception? FooError</code>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>[BlexEffect] Task OnFoo(A a, CancellationToken ct)</code></td>
                    <td>the above, plus <code>public void CancelFoo()</code> - and note the token is <em>not</em> on the public signature</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Reserved names</h2>
    <p>
        A generated member may not take one of these - they are inherited from <code>BlexStoreBase</code>
        or emitted by the generator itself. Collisions are reported as <code>BLEX005</code>.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Code="@Reserved" Language="text" Title="Reserved" Compact="true" />

    <h2>JSON conventions</h2>
    <p>
        Snapshots use <code>BlexJson.Options</code>: <code>JsonSerializerDefaults.Web</code>,
        case-insensitive property matching and enums written as strings. Slices are keyed by the
        generated <em>property</em> name (<code>Count</code>, not <code>_count</code>), and the global
        tree is keyed by store name.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock Code="@JsonShape" Language="json" />

